caption: $:/tags/hypergsd/ListItem/Prefix and /Suffix
title: ListItem Prefix and Suffix

! Summary
Add a fragment to ''every'' list row — before the title (Prefix) or after it (Suffix).

! Detail
Tag any tiddler with `$:/tags/hypergsd/ListItem/Prefix` or `$:/tags/hypergsd/ListItem/Suffix`. Its body renders in every row of every `$hgsd.list`, project view and contact view:

```
title: My due-date fragment
tags: Documentation [[HyperGSD API]]

<%if [is[current]tag[$:/GSD/Action]!field:due[]] %>
<span class="gsd-muted">due {{!!due}}</span>
<%endif%>
```

* `currentTiddler` inside a fragment is the row's item.
* ''Suppression signals'': `storyTiddler` holds the tiddler whose view the row renders inside (snapshotted by the core ViewTemplate before any list loop redefines `currentTiddler`; unset outside the story river) — a match with a row-item field means "this row already lives on that tiddler's page". `current-group` holds the grouped list's heading value (ambient only in the grouped branch; every shipped grouping is by `gsd_project` or `gsd_contact`) — a match means the heading already links there. The built-in jump links (`project-link`, and the contacts sub-plugin's `contact-link`) use both to hide exactly where the target is already on screen; their tooltip is the target tiddler's title.
* Fragments must ''self-gate'' — render nothing when they do not apply, like the seven built-in fragments in `$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/ui/list-items/` (complete, status, comp-date, body-text, realm, project-link, delete).
* ''Ordering'': the engine's tag-list order — any tag-tiddler `list` first, then member `list-before`/`list-after` pins, unlisted fragments appending alphabetically. The plugin ships a `list` on the Suffix tag tiddler pinning `comp-date → body-text → realm → project-link → delete`; the priorities sub-plugin's select pins itself after the status pills with a `list-after` on the fragment. A user-level `list` field on either tag tiddler overrides both.
* Adding or editing a fragment updates open views immediately; ''removing'' one takes effect on the next view refresh (frozen views cannot match a tiddler that no longer exists).
* ''Interactive fragments'' (a `<$reveal>`, a picker) declare their state and temp tiddlers in a `hgsd-refresh-whitelist` field on the fragment tiddler — single bracketed runs, space-separated — and the engine composes them into the row's freeze gate and every gate above the rows, so one field covers dashboards, views and the placement slot (see [[Refresh gates|Refresh gates]]). Alternatively, keep state under prefixes the chassis gates already admit (`$:/state/hypergsd/*`, `$:/state/popup/pick-*`, `$:/config/hypergsd/*`). Prefix runs only, never a literal `[[title]]` run (it emits unconditionally and defeats the gate). The worked examples are the contexts sub-plugin's contextualise fragment (`$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd-contexts/ui/list-items/context`) and, for a Strip member, the contacts sub-plugin's filter picker (`$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd-contacts/ui/components/contact-select`).

! Best Practice
Keep fragments cheap: they render once per row per list, so avoid filters over the whole wiki inside them.

!! Fragment layout contract

The row (`.gsd-list-item`) is a centred flex container: a fragment's content is vertically centred automatically — no wrapper class is needed. Root your fragment in a ''div'' or ''span'' so it receives the row's shrink protection (the title link is the only row child that flexes). Use `align-self` on your root element if you need a different alignment.